# Example ReRDMFT input file: carbon monoxide (R = 1.128 Angstrom), cc-pVDZ basis (co-cc-pvdz.gbs, from
# https://www.basissetexchange.org/, includes D shells), GNOF with 3 coupling subspaces of 2 orbitals each,
# FULL_OPTIMIZATION with the second-order NEO orbital optimizer and CHOLESKY TRUE: the AO integrals are decomposed
# once into Cholesky vectors and nothing of size n^4 is ever stored (see README.md, CHOLESKY).
# C4_SPINOR path (4-component Dirac-Hartree-Fock, RKB basis of 112 spinors, no-pair orbital rotations on the 56
# positive-energy spinors only). The RKB integrals come from ONE Cholesky decomposition of the real AO
# {Large-Large} u {Small-Small} Coulomb matrix (1409 vectors, ~50 s of the setup). Measured: ~4 min, ~0.9 GB
# peak, converges in 8 macro-iterations to -113.0044414 Ha (a genuine minimum). Follow the run with
# `tail -f co_ccpvdz_c4_gnof_neo_cholesky.live`.
NELEC 14
BASIS co-cc-pvdz.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 3
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO
CHOLESKY TRUE

GEOMETRY
C   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
O   0.000000   0.000000   1.128000
END
